 "issue": 711,
 "issue_title": "Bug: from_pandas silently drops columns when labels stringify to the same name",
 "issue_body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`from_pandas()` only checks duplicate labels before converting labels to strings. If two distinct pandas labels become the same string, the later column overwrites the earlier one in the Python `columns` dict before the frame reaches the C++ binding.\r\n\r\n## Evidence / audit context\r\n\r\n- Audit target: latest `origin/main` at `3ebc37cae0c2dc6a1b0d83c62eac468d83f1242f`.\r\n- Severity: **Critical**.\r\n- Relevant paths: `arnio/convert.py`, `bindings/bind_arnio.cpp`.\r\n- Audit probe on latest main converted a DataFrame with columns `[1, \"1\"]` into a single Arnio column named `\"1\"`, preserving only the second column's values.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\nimport arnio as ar\r\n\r\ndf = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2]], columns=[1, \"1\"])\r\nframe = ar.from_pandas(df)\r\nprint(frame.columns)\r\nprint(ar.to_pandas(frame).to_dict(\"list\"))\r\n```\r\n\r\nActual result: one column `['1']` with value `[2]`.\r\nExpected result: either both columns are preserved with unambiguous names, or `from_pandas()` raises a clear `ValueError`.\r\n\r\n## Why this matters\r\n\r\nThis can produce incorrect data, delayed runtime failures, or misleading API behavior. Arnio is a data preparation library, so silent corruption or unclear validation errors are especially risky for downstream pandas, sklearn, and data-quality workflows.\r\n\r\n## Suggested fix\r\n\r\nValidate duplicate labels after `str(col_name)` normalization, before inserting into `columns` or `dtype_hints`. The error should name the original labels that collide after string conversion.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] `from_pandas(pd.DataFrame([[1, 2]], columns=[1, \"1\"]))` raises a clear `ValueError`.\r\n- [ ] Existing duplicate-label validation still works for native duplicate pandas labels.\r\n- [ ] A regression test covers non-string labels that stringify to the same name.\r\n- [ ] No existing valid `from_pandas()` round-trips regress.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nThis issue was created from a manual end-to-end audit and includes a minimal repro where applicable.\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/711",
 "pr": 726,
 "pr_title": "fix(pandas): reject stringified column label collisions",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\n- reject pandas column labels that collide after Arnio stringifies them\n- keep existing duplicate-label rejection intact\n- add regression coverage for integer/string and bool/string label collisions\n\n## Verification\n- `python -m pytest tests/test_convert.py -v --tb=short`\n- `python -m pytest tests/ -v --tb=short` (`634 passed, 1 skipped`)\n- `ruff check .`\n- `black --check .`\n- CMake native build + `test_column_consistency.exe`\n\nCloses #711",
